Package: tidyfault
Title: Fault Tree Analysis in R with Tidyverse Coding
Version: 0.0.0.9
Authors@R: 
    c(person("Timothy", "Fraser", , "timothy.fraser.1@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
             comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4509-0244")),
      person("Jingyao", "Tong", , "jingyaotong6@gmail.com", role = c("aut"),
             comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0009-6147-756X")))
Description: Fault tree analysis with tidy data. Represents a fault tree as
    tables of nodes and edges, uses 'tidygraph' and 'ggraph' to lay out and draw
    it, and derives minimal cut sets and top event probabilities. Evaluates
    binary and probabilistic scenarios, and simulates random fault trees.
URL: https://tidyfault.netlify.app, https://github.com/timothyfraser/tidyfault
BugReports: https://github.com/timothyfraser/tidyfault/issues
